### ring, hole (engine refuses), then turn
   ring1   guard built 
           shipped built 
   hole1   guard refused Hole 1 could not be built by this engine, so it is shown without it.
           shipped refused hole1 (hole): solidcraft refused it -- solid.cylinder: the cut could not be computed reliably: it came out empty. The result was refused rather than kept wrong; where the bodies only touch (faces flush with each other), overlapping them slightly usually helps (refined tolerance 1.693712e-2 mm)
   turn1   guard refused Turn 1 is not built because Hole 1, which it uses, was refused.
           shipped refused turn1 (rotate): its target hole1 was refused (hole1 (hole): solidcraft refused it -- solid.cylinder: the cut could not be computed reliably: it came out empty. The result was refused rather than kept wrong; where the bodies only touch (faces flush with each other), overlapping them slightly usually helps (refined tolerance 1.693712e-2 mm))
